  "text": "Lauren Smith-Oskrochi | Austin Veterinary Emergency & Specialty (AVES)\nSkip to Primary Content\nContact Us\nContact Us\nMap\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway,\nBuilding A,\nAustin,\nTX,\n78731\nCall\n(512) 343-2837\nEmergency\nEmergency\nPhone:\n(512) 343-2837\nAddress:\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway,\nBuilding A,\nAustin,\nTX,\n78731\nPay Online\nCareers\nAbout Us\nAbout AVES\nOur Team\nCareers\nAngel Fund\nNews & Blog\nServices\nEmergency\nAnesthesiology\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDiagnostic Imaging\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology & Endoscopy\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nAVES Oncology Group\nSurgery & Orthopedics\nView all Services\nPet Owners\nFAQ\nPrescription Refill Form\nPatient Forms\nPay Online\nFinancing\nReferring Veterinarians\nReferral Portal\nReferral Form\nCase Studies\nContinuing Education\nLunch & Learns\nEmergency\nContact Us\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nLauren Smith-Oskrochi\nDVM, DAVCR (RO)\nLauren Smith-Oskrochi\nDr. Lauren Smith-Oskrochi is a board-certified veterinary radiation oncologist with specialized expertise in advanced, image-guided radiation therapy and quality-of-life centered cancer care. She joins AVES after serving as a Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiation Oncology at the Texas A&M School of Veterinary Medicine & Biomedical Sciences, where she mentored oncology residents, interns, and veterinary students while advancing clinical research on innovative radiation therapy applications for both neoplastic and non-neoplastic diseases.\nDr. Smith-Oskrochi completed her radiation oncology residency at the University of Wisconsin–Madison and has since built a career focused on highly precise treatment planning, multidisciplinary collaboration, and compassionate communication with families and referring veterinarians. Her clinical interests include low dose radiation therapy for non-neoplastic diseases, pre-operative radiation and multi-modal therapy, and the development of novel immobilization devices to further improve accuracy and patient comfort. She has authored multiple peer-reviewed publications and has served as a primary research mentor for numerous oncology residents.\nAt AVES, Dr. Smith-Oskrochi is committed to delivering personalized, evidence-based radiation therapy with an emphasis on minimizing side effects and supporting each patient’s comfort throughout treatment. She values clear, collaborative communication with primary care veterinarians and strives to make radiation therapy accessible, reassuring, and tailored to the goals of every family.\nOutside the hospital, Dr. Smith-Oskrochi stays busy enjoying life in Austin with her husband, their two young daughters, and a lively household of three cats and two dogs.\nContact Us\nAbout AVES\nView all Services\nPatient Forms\nReferral Portal\nContact Us\nPhone:\n(512) 343-2837\nFax:\n(512) 343-2844\nAddress:\n7501 North Capital of Texas Highway\nBuilding A\nAustin\n,\nTX\n78731\nHours of Operation\nMain Hours\nMon\nOpen 24 hrs\nTue\nOpen 24 hrs\nWed\nOpen 24 hrs\nThu\nOpen 24 hrs\nFri\nOpen 24 hrs\nSat\nOpen 24 hrs\nSun\nOpen 24 hrs\nOpen 24/7/365 for Pet Emergencies, Specialty Services Available by Appointment Only.\n©\nCopyright\n2026\nAccessibility\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nCookie Preferences",
